      },
      "text": "While the Duke group began to distribute Cozyduke in an increasingly aggressive manner, Seaduke installations were reserved only for select targets.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_7",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Forkmeiamfamous_SeaDuke",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s7"
      },
      "text": "Background The group behind Seaduke is a cyberespionage operation that is responsible for a series of attacks against high-profile individuals and organizations in government, international policy and private research in the United States and Europe.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_8",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Forkmeiamfamous_SeaDuke",
      "locator": {
        "page": 1,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p1_s8"
      },
      "text": "It has a range of malware tools at its disposal, known as the Dukes, including Cozyduke ( Trojan.Cozer ), Miniduke ( Backdoor.Miniduke ) and Cosmicduke ( Backdoor.Tinybaron ).",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_9",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Forkmeiamfamous_SeaDuke",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s1"
      },
      "text": "News of the Duke group first emerged in March and April of 2015, when reports detailing attacks involving a sophisticated threat actor variously called Office Monkeys, EuroAPT , Cozy Bear , and Cozyduke were published .",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_11",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Forkmeiamfamous_SeaDuke",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s3"
      },
      "text": "The group began its current campaign as early as March 2014, when Trojan.Cozer (aka Cozyduke) was identified on the network of a private research institute in Washington, D.C.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_12",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Forkmeiamfamous_SeaDuke",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s4"
      },
      "text": "In the months that followed, the Duke group began to target victims with â€œOffice Monkeysâ€​- and â€œeFaxâ€​-themed emails, booby-trapped with a Cozyduke payload.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_14",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Forkmeiamfamous_SeaDuke",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s6"
      },
      "text": "The Duke group has mounted an extended campaign targeting high-profile networks over extended periods, something which is far beyond the reach of the majority of threat actors.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_15",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Forkmeiamfamous_SeaDuke",
      "locator": {
