        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s7"
      },
      "text": "Attack infrastructure leveraging hundreds of compromised websites Rapidly developed malware frameworks in concurrent use Sophisticated operators with fine-tuned computer network exploitation (CNE) skills",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_16",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Forkmeiamfamous_SeaDuke",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s8"
      },
      "text": "Although Cozyduke activity was first identified in March 2014, it wasnâ€™t until July that the group managed to successfully compromise high-profile government networks.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_17",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "Forkmeiamfamous_SeaDuke",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s9"
      },
      "text": "In parallel, the Duke group was also installing separate malware onto these networks, namely Backdoor.Miniduke and the more elusive Trojan.Seaduke .",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
